{"paper": "2024-Tier1-26-Sep-2024-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Annual income of five schools (in lakhs) In case of how many schools, the income by semester fee, is less than three times of donation?", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The following table shows the percentage distribution of students in four different schools during the years 2021-22. If there was a total number of 16,000 and 18,000 students during the years 2021 and 2022 respectively, then the difference in number of students in school 4 in 2022 with respect to 2021 is:", "options": [{"text": "240", "added": false}, {"text": "280", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}, {"text": "380", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "(a) and (b)", "added": false}, {"text": "(b), (c) and (d)", "added": false}, {"text": "(a), (b) and (d)", "added": false}, {"text": "(a) and (c)", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "One pipe can fill a tank four times as fast as another pipe. If together the two pipes can fill the tank in 48 minutes, the slower pipe alone will be able to fill the tank in:", "options": [{"text": "192 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "288 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "240 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "144 minutes", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "A number whose fifth part increased by 5 is equal to its third part decreased by 7. Find half of the number.", "options": [{"text": "45", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "764.71 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "704.00 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "682.60 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "714.05 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "Two successive percentage decrease of 25% each is by what percentage less than two successive percentage increase of 25% each? (Round to two decimal places.)", "options": [{"text": "50%", "added": false}, {"text": "43.75%", "added": false}, {"text": "22.22%", "added": false}, {"text": "56.25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "If (48°+ k) is an acute angle and sin(48°+ k) = cos13°, what is the value of k(in °)?", "options": [{"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "23", "added": false}, {"text": "29", "added": false}, {"text": "37", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "If the angles of a triangle are in the ratio 7 : 8 : 3, then the value of the largest angle is:", "options": [{"text": "120°", "added": false}, {"text": "80°", "added": false}, {"text": "100°", "added": false}, {"text": "60°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Evaluate the given expression.", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2020 and 2021", "added": false}, {"text": "2018 and 2019", "added": false}, {"text": "2017 and 2018", "added": false}, {"text": "2018 and 2020", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "13 : 9", "added": false}, {"text": "13 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "11 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "11 : 9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "In a room, there are some chairs and some people. If on each chair, only one person is seated, then there is no chair for exactly one person. If on each chair, two persons sit, then there is one vacant chair. What is the number of chairs in the room?", "options": [{"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "A person first increases the price of a commodity by 8% and then he announces a discount of 18%. The actual discount (in%) on the original price is:", "options": [{"text": "11.44", "added": false}, {"text": "14.44", "added": false}, {"text": "9.44", "added": false}, {"text": "8.44", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "Two athletes are participating in a race on a circular track of 220 m. Ravi runs at the speed of 22 m/s, while Kapil runs at the speed of 11 m/s. They start from the same point, at the same time and in the same direction. After how many seconds will they meet for the first time?", "options": [{"text": "15 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "16 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "20 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "24 seconds", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "circular-track", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "If books bought at prices ranging from ₹200 to ₹260 are sold at prices ranging from ₹250 to 300, what is the greatest possible profit that might be made in selling 25 books?", "options": [{"text": "₹2,300", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,800", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,700", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "Three people, A, B and C, invest in a business in the ratio 2 : 3 : 5. It was decided that 9% of the profits will go to charity. If the total profit was ₹2,50,000, then find the share of C in the profit (in ₹).", "options": [{"text": "1,26,950", "added": false}, {"text": "1,11,650", "added": false}, {"text": "1,21,850", "added": false}, {"text": "1,13,750", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "In a class of 150 students (boys and girls only), the girls are 60. The average weight of boys is 52 kg and that of girls is 48 kg. What is the average weight (in kg) of the whole class?", "options": [{"text": "50.4", "added": false}, {"text": "48.8", "added": false}, {"text": "49.6", "added": false}, {"text": "51.2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "96", "added": false}, {"text": "98", "added": false}, {"text": "112", "added": false}, {"text": "108", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "7,850", "added": false}, {"text": "8,164", "added": false}, {"text": "7,693", "added": false}, {"text": "7,536", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "If ₹1,875 becomes ₹2,625 in 4 years, what will ₹24,000 become at the end of 9 years at the same rate of interest, under simple interest?", "options": [{"text": "₹45,600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹21,600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹34,800", "added": false}, {"text": "₹43,200", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "Given a linear equation in two variables: 5x + 7y - 8 = 0, which of the following linear equations, along with the given equation, forms a system of linear equations having no solution?", "options": [{"text": "5x + 7y - 16 = 0", "added": false}, {"text": "7x + 5y - 8 = 0", "added": false}, {"text": "5x - 7y - 8 = 0", "added": false}, {"text": "10x + 14y - 16 = 0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "Find the remainder when 920 + 2 is divided by 4.", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "From a point A, which is at a distance of 17 cm from the centre C of a circle with radius 8 cm, the pair of tangents AB and AD to the circle are drawn. The area of the quadrilateral ABCD is _____ cm2.", "options": [{"text": "192", "added": false}, {"text": "120", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "360", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}]}